## 5. Contract surface

Primary barrel:

```text
runtime/bus/actionEventLog/actionEventLogStoreContract.mjs
```

Exports include:

```text
ACTION_EVENT_LOG_STORE_CONTRACT_VERSION
ACTION_EVENT_LOG_DEFAULT_DURABLE_EVENT_TYPES
ACTION_EVENT_LOG_HIGH_VOLUME_EVENT_TYPES
isDefaultDurableActionEventLogType(...)
isHighVolumeActionEventLogType(...)
normalizeActionEventLogAppendEntry(...)
validateActionEventLogAppendEntry(...)
assertActionEventLogAppendEntry(...)
copyActionEventLogEntry(...)
normalizeActionEventLogReadFilter(...)
validateActionEventLogReadFilter(...)
normalizeActionEventLogReadOptions(...)
validateActionEventLogReadOptions(...)
validateActionEventLogStoreAdapter(...)
assertActionEventLogStoreAdapter(...)
validateActionEventLogAppendResult(...)
assertActionEventLogAppendResult(...)
validateActionEventLogReadResult(...)
assertActionEventLogReadResult(...)
```

Contract version:

```text
runtime.actionEventLogStore.v1
```

Default durable-log eligible event types:

```text
action.accepted
action.started
action.completed
action.failed
action.cancelled
action.timeout
action.policyDenied
```

High-volume event types excluded by default:

```text
action.stream.delta
```

`action.stream.delta` is recognized by the contract but accepted only when the caller explicitly passes:

```js
{ includeHighVolumeEvents: true }
```

This is a contract policy only. The runtime still does not retain, replay, or persist stream deltas.

---

## 6. Adapter contract shape

A future event-log adapter must satisfy this shape:

```js
{
    contractVersion: "runtime.actionEventLogStore.v1",
    adapterId: "event-log.some-adapter",
    capabilities: {
        append: true,
        read: true,
        cursorRead: true,
        highVolumeEvents: false
    },
    appendEvent(entry) {},
    readEvents(filter, options) {}
}
```

Append result shape:

```js
{
    accepted: true,
    eventId,
    sequence,
    logOffset,
    storedAt
}
```

Read result shape:

```js
{
    events: [],
    cursor: {
        lastSequence,
        lastLogOffset
    },
    truncated: false
}
```

Cursor policy:

```text
sequence      numeric cursor compatible with the existing event-history sequence style
logOffset     opaque durable-backend cursor token, when a future backend supports it
```

The contract does not require every future backend to support both cursor styles.

