## 9. Caveats / known risks

### Finding: Contract exists but runtime persistence is not wired

Affected surface:

```text
future eventLogStoreBackend, durable audit trail, restart recovery
```

Why it matters:

```text
This branch validates future adapter shape only. It does not make action events durable.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Use a separate runtime-event-log-store-integration plan/spec before wiring runtime publication into a store.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
future append failure policy, retry/buffer behavior, and whether action execution should ever fail because durable append fails
```

### Finding: Stream deltas remain high-volume / excluded by default

Affected surface:

```text
action.stream.delta retention, replay, durable storage volume, future graph observation
```

Why it matters:

```text
Durable stream-delta storage can create high write volume and ambiguous replay semantics.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Keep includeHighVolumeEvents false by default and require an explicit future retention/replay policy branch.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
future stream-delta sampling, coalescing, retention, cursor, and replay policy
```

### Finding: Cross-process pub/sub is still separate

Affected surface:

```text
future graph/control service hosting and external event listeners
```

Why it matters:

```text
Durable event logging and cross-process live fanout are different responsibilities.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Keep cross-process bridge/pub-sub as a separate plan/spec branch.
```

